      prompt: "Напиши статью (feature) для сайта школы журналистики о том, почему местная расследовательская журналистика важна и какие риски она несёт. Приведи пример (реальный или вымышленный) и предложи к статье заголовок в газетном стиле.",
      minWords: 250, use: ["whistleblower", "paper trail", "corroborate", "in the public interest"],
      model: "Headline: Town hall cash: who knew what?\n\nWhen people picture investigative journalism, they tend to imagine national scandals, secret meetings in car parks and documents leaked to famous reporters. Yet some of the most valuable investigations happen far from the capital, in small newsrooms with tiny budgets and a handful of determined staff.\n\nConsider a fictional but entirely plausible case. A whistleblower in a city council notices that the same building firm wins every major contract, regardless of price. She takes her suspicions to the local paper. A reporter spends months following the paper trail: company registers, council minutes, planning applications. Gradually a pattern emerges. The firm's owner turns out to be a close relative of a senior councillor, and the tenders were written in a way that only his company could satisfy.\n\nNone of this would matter if the paper simply printed rumours. The value of the work lies in the discipline behind it. Every allegation has to be checked, every claim needs a second source to corroborate it, and the people accused must be given a genuine chance to reply. That is what separates journalism in the public interest from gossip.\n\nThe risks, however, are real. Local papers rarely have lawyers on staff, and a single libel action can threaten their survival. Sources may lose their jobs, and reporters may find themselves unwelcome in the very community they serve.\n\nEven so, the alternative is worse. When nobody is watching how public money is spent, the temptation to misuse it grows. A well-sourced local investigation does not just expose one scandal; it reminds everyone in power that someone might be paying attention."
